HILL CANNON — REPRODUCTION SPECIFICATION
========================================
Single-file Python 3 game. Libraries: pygame, numpy.
An implementer should be able to rebuild the same game from this document alone.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PURPOSE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2D artillery game. Player cannon sits on a hill at LEFT. A packed city fills
the rest of the ground. Destroy enough of the city (campaign target) before
the player cannon takes 10 hits.

Win a siege:  destroyed_ratio >= current_win_ratio
Lose a siege: player_hp reaches 0
Quit: Esc or close window

destroyed_ratio:
  Each fully destroyed building (alive==False OR fall >= height) is worth 1.
  If it was the air-raid-siren building when it died (counted_double), worth 2.
  ratio = points / total_building_count

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. CAMPAIGN DIFFICULTY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Start: round_num = 1
current_win_ratio = min(1.00, 0.50 + 0.10 * (round_num - 1))
  Round 1 needs 50%, then 60%, 70% … capped at 100%.

enemy_accuracy_multiplier = 1.0 + 0.05 * (round_num - 1)
  Each successful surrender (WIN) adds +5% to enemy hit chance.

On WIN + continue (R):
  If current_win_ratio < 100%, increment round_num.
  Rebuild city. Player always gets 3 A-bombs and full HP.

On LOSE (player cannon destroyed):
  Immediately reset round_num = 1.
  Need returns to 50%. Enemy accuracy bonus returns to +0%.
  R starts a fresh siege from those starting values.

Every rebuilt siege (win or lose) starts with 3 A-bombs unless demo (6).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. WINDOW / TECH
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Internal sim: 1280 x 720. Draw to an off-screen Surface, then
pygame.transform.smoothscale onto the real window.

Window: pygame.RESIZABLE, min 640x360.
Persist {x,y,w,h} in shells_window.json next to the script.
Before set_mode, set SDL_VIDEO_WINDOW_POS from saved x,y (default 80,60).
Save geometry on VIDEORESIZE, WINDOWMOVED, every ~2s, and on quit.

Caption: "Hill Cannon — Level the City"
FPS 60. Mixer: 22050 Hz, 16-bit, stereo, ~24 channels.
Sounds: NumPy-generated PCM; make_sound needs a 2-D (N,2) int16 array.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. WORLD
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GROUND_Y = 650
Night-blue vertical sky gradient.
Distant darker skyline silhouettes behind the playable city (draw with a
fixed random.seed so they do not flicker).
Ground: green-brown strip, 6px lighter lip at GROUND_Y.
Hill: filled polygon on the LEFT, roughly ending near x=200.
Player mount: hill_peak = (90, GROUND_Y - 210). About 1.5x a mid-rise.

City starts x=210, packed to W-30.
Each building:
  width 22–48 px, gap 4–14 px
  stories random 1–40
  story_h = 14, height = stories * 14
  y = GROUND_Y - height
  muted slate/brown/green-gray, darker 6px right edge
  window grid ~6x8 px, columns ~12 px
  windows start mostly ON (warm 220,210,140), some OFF

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. CONTROLS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Left / Up        rotate barrel counter-clockwise
Right / Down     rotate barrel clockwise
Rotation         FULL 360 degrees, including straight down. Wrap angle.
1 / 2 / 3        muzzle force (default 2)
Space            fire normal shell
B                fire A-bomb (if any remain, or if unlimited)
U                toggle unlimited A-bombs for the human player
P                pause / unpause (simulation frozen; overlay "PAUSED")
R                after game-over: next siege (if won) or new campaign (if lost)
Any key          during DEMO: abort demo, start a new human campaign at round 1
Esc              quit

Fire rate: 3 shots/sec (cooldown 1/3 s), shared by shells and bombs.

Muzzle speeds: force 1=430, 2=640, 3=920 px/s
Gravity on all projectiles: +520 px/s^2 on vy

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. PLAYER CANNON
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Draw: dark circular mount + thick barrel 40px along angle + gold tip.
When HP hits 0: EXPLODE — rumble + fireball SFX, large fire burst, flying
metal chunks, then stop drawing the intact mount.

HP 10. Enemy shell within 38 px of hill_peak is a hit (−1 HP, red flash).
Player shells never hurt the player.

Health UI: a 160x14 bar top-left plus "HP n/10".
  >70% green, 40–70% yellow.
  RED AND BLINKING if HP <= 3 OR HP/10 < 0.40.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. SHELLS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Integrate: vy += GRAVITY*dt; x += vx*dt; y += vy*dt.
Die off-screen or at y >= GROUND_Y (dirt burst + boom).

Player shell: small gold circle, short gold trail.
Enemy shell: red/orange.
A-bomb: SAME ballistics as a normal shell at current force.
  Distinct look: large pulsing green warhead (~8–12 px), dark-green fins,
  lime core, green/yellow spark trail.

Collision order per shell:
  1) ground
  2) player mount (enemy shells only)
  3) air-raid SIREN hitbox if present
  4) rooftop GUN hitbox (non-bomb shells)
  5) building body rect

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8. BUILDINGS — DAMAGE, LIGHTS, FIRE, ARCS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5 body hits destroy a building unless a special kill applies.
Hits 1–4: crack lines on the facade.

On a body hit, near impact:
  nearby windows often go OUT
  others DIM (25–75%) or FLICKER
  chance to black out several floors
  chance whole building blacks out, higher when 1–2 hits from collapse
    (~8% normal, ~38% at 2 remaining, ~55% at 1 remaining)
  ~55% chance a small ember fire at impact lasting 5–10 s

Direct hit on rooftop GUN: instant destroy (cannon-kill).
Direct hit on SIREN: instant destroy + double score + stop air-raid +
  topple with doubled smash power.

Kill outcomes:
  10% of ordinary kills TOPPLE like an A-bomb.
  A-bomb and siren kills ALWAYS topple.
  Other kills pancake-drop straight down with base dust.
  ~25% of non-topple kills (and gun/bomb kills) are fiery.

Pancake: rect sinks down; gone when fall >= height.

Electrical arcing:
  After a body hit, ~22% chance the living building starts arcing.
  Every 3–5 s zap a spatially adjacent living neighbor (jagged bolt + zap SFX).
  ~72% of bolts start a fire on the target.
  4 arc-fires on one building = 1 shell-equivalent hit.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9. TOPPLE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Direction: from impact vs building center, else toward the denser side.

Split facade into horizontal slabs (~2 stories). Each slab is a Chunk:
  vx in fall direction (stronger higher up), slight vy, spin, gravity,
  weak ground bounce, continuous smoke/junk. Long rumble + boom.

Neighbor smash by city INDEX (buildings sorted by center-x), only in the
fall direction:
  Adjacent (index distance 1):
    several body hits (power 3, or 5 if A-bomb; doubled if siren kill)
    A-bomb/siren may chain-topple neighbor (~40% if power >= 5)
  1–2 buildings farther (index distance 2 or 3):
    light: TWO arc-fires OR ONE body hit
  Farther: no smash

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10. ENEMY ROOFTOP GUNS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Count scales with how close the city is to the CURRENT win ratio:
  2 guns at 0% progress toward the target
  5 guns when destroyed_ratio / win_ratio ~= 1
  interpolate and round

Place new guns on the tallest living buildings that lack one.
On placement: silent 4–8 seconds, then fire every 1.4 s.

Aim:
  Barrel may use any 0–360 angle but MUST face the player
  (dot(barrel_dir, vector_to_hill) > 0.05). Never fire the opposite way.
  Independently pick force 1/2/3.
  Simulate ballistic arcs. If the path hits another living building first,
  do NOT fire; keep changing elevation until a clear loft exists.
  After 3 friendly-fire impacts, HOLD until a path can reach the player
  without hitting the city.

Accuracy when they fire:
  Base chance to use the exact player-hit solution = 1/7
  Scale by building height:
    40 stories *0.98, 20 *0.50, 10 *0.25, 1 *~0.12; interpolate
  Then multiply by enemy_accuracy_multiplier from §2.
  Cap at 1.0.
  Missed shots jitter angle but still face the player and still reject
  predicted friendly hits.

Visual: small dark roof mount + barrel + gold tip.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11. AIR-RAID SIREN
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Exactly ONE building per city (prefer stories >= 12) has a red pulsing
rooftop siren (lamp + horns). Hitbox ~22x24 above the roof.

On city create: start a LOOPING rising/falling wail (~420–800 Hz over
~3.2 s, modest volume). Stop when that building dies, on win/lose/quit,
or when a new city is built.

Hitting the siren: instant topple, 2x score, stop wail, doubled smash.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12. A-BOMBS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Human: 3 per rebuilt city. B fires one at current force.
U toggles unlimited (HUD shows INF; B never decrements).
Demo gunner: 6 bombs per demo siege and SHOULD spend them on sirens,
guns, and buildings with stories >= 12.

One A-bomb hit destroys the building and ALWAYS topples it.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
13. DEMO / ATTRACT MODE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
After 10 seconds IDLE on a human game-over screen (no keys/mouse), start
demo from round 1 with a new city.

Demo player is a PERFECT gunner:
  Prioritize living SIREN, then rooftop GUNS (tallest first), then tallest
  remaining building. KEEP that focus until the building is destroyed.
  Solve exact ballistics from hill_peak to the aim point (siren lamp, gun,
  or upper facade). Rotate the player barrel to that solution (360° ok).
  Fire when the barrel is close. Use A-bombs as in §12.
  If several shots in a row destroy nothing: drop focus, change loft /
  aim offset, pick a new solution. Repeat until something dies.

Demo climbs the same campaign ladder (need +10%, enemy acc +5% per win).
Demo STOPS and a NEW HUMAN campaign starts at round 1 when:
  - demo player cannon is destroyed, OR
  - demo WINS a siege whose requirement was already 100%, OR
  - the human presses any key during demo.

Short ~1.2 s pause between demo rounds so the result is visible.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
14. AUDIO (procedural, several variants, random pick + volume jitter)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cannon fire: 30–70 Hz boom + 25–45 ms muzzle crack + faint 380–560 Hz ring
Shell impact: crack then 0.5–0.8 s bass rumble
Collapse: grind + thud
Topple / A-bomb / player death: longer 0.9–1.4 s deep rumble + explosion
Building crack: short snap
Electrical arc: harsh AM buzz 900–1600 Hz + hiss + pops
Air raid: looping sweep described in §11
Player hit: dull ~36 Hz thump
Fireball whoosh for fiery collapses
Win / lose stingers
Dedicated mixer channel for the looping siren

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
15. VISUAL FX
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Shell trails, impact bursts, ember flames, jagged lightning, rotating
topple chunks, player-hit red overlay (~0.25 s), player-cannon explosion
chunks. Pause overlay. Demo banner: "DEMO — PERFECT PLAYER".

HUD bottom example:
  Need 50%   Have 12.3%   Round 1   Guns 2   Acc +0%   Bombs 3
Also show force pips and A-bomb pips (or INF).

Game-over (human only):
  WIN: "CITY SURRENDERS — YOU WIN"
       R next siege (+10% city, +5% enemy acc); at 100% "another 100% siege"
  LOSE: "CANNON DESTROYED — YOU LOSE"
        R new siege from 50% / base accuracy
  Hint: idle 10s = demo, P pause, U bombs, ESC

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
16. MAIN LOOP
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Events -> pause check -> aim keys (human) or demo_think ->
ensure_cannons -> update buildings (and enemy fire) ->
update shells -> collide ->
update embers/particles/bolts/chunks ->
draw world, FX, cannon/HP, HUD, banners -> present scaled -> save geom.

If paused: still draw, skip simulation.
If game_over: buildings may keep falling; idle timer or demo advance.

Gameplay coordinates always stay in 1280x720 space after resize.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
17. RESET HELPERS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
begin_siege(reset_campaign, as_demo):
  optional round_num = 1
  new city + siren + air-raid
  clear shells/particles/embers/bolts/chunks
  HP=10, bombs=6 if demo else 3, force=2, angle=-0.55
  player_exploded=False, demo focus cleared
  place starting enemy guns (2) with 4–8 s silence

First launch: begin_siege(reset_campaign=True, as_demo=False)